            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous transcatheter obliteration of aortic paravalvular leak.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>80-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 76-year-old man who underwent aortic valve replacement for severe calcific aortic stenosis developed a significant paravalvular leak. Because the risk of re-operation was felt too great, a percutaneous transcatheter obliteration of the defect using an Amplatzer vascular plug was undertaken, with an excellent clinical outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
